IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 12 Division 1, first half: s 386A (words used in ss 387B, 387C, 397 and 401), s 387 (serving a
-- document on a company), ss 387A to 387D (sending notices and documents by electronic communications). Part agent sgo.
--
-- Where a subsection opens "Where ... a notice is required or permitted to be given ... to a member, officer or auditor", the
-- opening is a "where" gate on a "may": the Guide's periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), says a failed "where" answers JUST FALSE, and
-- the grant line points the other way. This module leaves the answer as the periods ruling gives it, and each such site is a fork line in
-- NOTES.md (split site type (ii)). Where the gate is "if" or "with ...", a failed gate answers NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12).

DECLARE `s 387B(6)(a) kind of thing sent` IS ONE OF
    `s 387B(6)(a)(i) a share certificate`
    `s 387B(6)(a)(ii) a debenture`
    `s 387B(6)(a)(iii) a certificate of any other interest in a company`
    `s 387B(6)(a)(iv) an instrument of transfer of any share, debenture or other interest in a company`
    `s 387B(6)(a) something else`

§ `Section 386A: the words used in ss 387B, 387C, 397 and 401`

-- src:27074 | 386A. In this section and sections 387B, 387C, 397 and 401, unless
-- src:27075 | the contrary intention appears —
-- src:27076 | “consolidated financial statements” and “parent company” have
-- src:27077 | the meanings given by section 209A;
@ref s 386A (src:27074-27077)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 386A, 387B, 387C, 397 or 401` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the term is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term is "consolidated financial statements" or "parent company"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386A the meaning of the term is the meaning given by section 209A` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term is used in section 386A, 387B, 387C, 397 or 401`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 387B, 387C, 397 and 401"
    ELSE (IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the term is used`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the contrary intention appears"
          ELSE (IF `the term is "consolidated financial statements" or "parent company"`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks only of those two terms

-- "financial statements" means the financial statements of a company required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards and, in the case
-- of a parent company, means the consolidated financial statements. (s 209A, which defines "parent company", belongs to another part: the fact is an input.)
-- src:27074 | 386A. In this section and sections 387B, 387C, 397 and 401, unless
-- src:27075 | the contrary intention appears —
-- src:27082 | “financial statements” means the financial statements of a
-- src:27083 | company required to be prepared by the Accounting
-- src:27084 | Standards and, in the case of a parent company, means the
-- src:27085 | consolidated financial statements.
@ref s 386A (src:27074-27085)
GIVEN `the term is used in section 386A, 387B, 387C, 397 or 401` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the term is used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company as section 209A defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are the financial statements of the company required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are the consolidated financial statements of the parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386A "financial statements" the statements are the financial statements` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term is used in section 386A, 387B, 387C, 397 or 401`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and sections 387B, 387C, 397 and 401"
    ELSE (IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the term is used`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the contrary intention appears"
          ELSE (IF `the company is a parent company as section 209A defines the term`
                THEN (IF `the statements are the consolidated financial statements of the parent company`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a parent company, means the consolidated financial statements"
                ELSE (IF `the statements are the financial statements of the company required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"financial statements\" means the financial statements of a company required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards"

§ `Section 387: service of documents on a company`

-- src:27091 | 387. A document may be served on a company by leaving it at or
-- src:27092 | sending it by registered post to the registered office of the company.
@ref s 387 (src:27091-27092)
GIVEN `the document is left at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is sent by registered post to the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387 the document is served on the company` MEANS
    IF `the document is left at the registered office of the company` OR `the document is sent by registered post to the registered office of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document may be served on a company by leaving it at or sending it by registered post to the registered office"; the section does not say "only", and other ways of service may be given elsewhere

§ `Section 387A: electronic transmission of notices of meetings`

§§ `Section 387A(1): sending the notice by electronic communications`

-- src:27096 | 387A.—(1) Where any notice of a meeting is required or permitted
-- src:27097 | to be given, sent or served under this Act or under the constitution of a
-- src:27098 | company by the company or the directors of the company to —
-- src:27100 | (a) a member of the company; or
-- src:27102 | (b) an officer or auditor of the company,
-- src:27104 | that notice may be given, sent or served using electronic
-- src:27105 | communications to the current address of that person.
@ref s 387A(1) (src:27096-27105)
GIVEN `the notice of a meeting is required or permitted to be given, sent or served under this Act or under the constitution of the company by the company or the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given, sent or served using electronic communications to the current address of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387A(1) the notice may be given, sent or served using electronic communications to the current address of the person` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the notice of a meeting is required or permitted to be given, sent or served under this Act or under the constitution of the company by the company or the directors of the company`
            AND (`the person is a member of the company` OR `the person is an officer or auditor of the company`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "Where" gate of the subsection (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b): "a \"where ...\" condition: when it fails the answer is `JUST FALSE`"); split site type (ii), fork F-387A-1
    ELSE (IF `the notice is given, sent or served using electronic communications to the current address of the person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that notice may be given, sent or served using electronic communications to the current address of that person"; the subsection grants that way and says nothing of any other

§§ `Section 387A(2) and (3): notice published on a website`

-- src:27109 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a notice of a meeting is also
-- src:27110 | treated as given or sent to, or served on a person where —
-- src:27112 | (a) the company and that person have agreed in writing that
-- src:27113 | notices of meetings required to be given to that person may
-- src:27114 | instead be accessed by the person on a website;
-- src:27116 | (b) the meeting is a meeting to which that agreement applies;
-- src:27118 | (c) the notice is published on the website such that it is or can
-- src:27119 | be made legible;
-- src:27121 | (d) that person is notified, in a manner for the time being
-- src:27122 | agreed between the person and the company for the
-- src:27123 | purpose, of —
-- src:27125 | (i) the publication of the notice on that website;
-- src:27127 | (ii) the address of that website; and
-- src:27132 | (iii) the place on that website where the notice may be
-- src:27133 | accessed, and how it may be accessed; and
-- src:27135 | (e) the notice continues to be published on and remains
-- src:27136 | accessible to that person from that website throughout the
-- src:27137 | period beginning with the giving of that notification and
-- src:27138 | ending with the conclusion of the meeting.
@ref s 387A(2) (src:27109-27138)
GIVEN `the company and the person have agreed in writing that notices of meetings required to be given to the person may instead be accessed by the person on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting to which that agreement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is published on the website such that it is or can be made legible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed between the person and the company for the purpose, of the publication of the notice on that website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed between the person and the company for the purpose, of the address of that website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed between the person and the company for the purpose, of the place on that website where the notice may be accessed, and how it may be accessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice continues to be published on and remains accessible to the person from that website throughout the period beginning with the giving of that notification and ending with the conclusion of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387A(2) the notice of a meeting is treated as given, sent or served by publication on a website` MEANS
    IF    `the company and the person have agreed in writing that notices of meetings required to be given to the person may instead be accessed by the person on a website`
       AND `the meeting is a meeting to which that agreement applies`
       AND `the notice is published on the website such that it is or can be made legible`
       AND `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed between the person and the company for the purpose, of the publication of the notice on that website`
       AND `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed between the person and the company for the purpose, of the address of that website`
       AND `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed between the person and the company for the purpose, of the place on that website where the notice may be accessed, and how it may be accessed`
       AND `the notice continues to be published on and remains accessible to the person from that website throughout the period beginning with the giving of that notification and ending with the conclusion of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a notice of a meeting is also treated as given ... where (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ...; and (e) ..." (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); the function is named for this route, so JUST FALSE says only that this route is not made out

-- src:27140 | (3) For the purposes of this Act, a notice of a meeting treated in
-- src:27141 | accordance with subsection (2) as given or sent to or served on any
-- src:27142 | person is treated as so given, sent or served at the time of the
-- src:27143 | notification mentioned in subsection (2)(d).
@ref s 387A(3) (src:27140-27143)
GIVEN `the notice of a meeting is treated in accordance with subsection (2) as given, sent or served on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the notification mentioned in subsection (2)(d)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 387A(3) the day on which the notice is treated as given, sent or served` MEANS
    IF `the notice of a meeting is treated in accordance with subsection (2) as given, sent or served on the person`
    THEN JUST `the day of the notification mentioned in subsection (2)(d)`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a notice of a meeting treated in accordance with subsection (2) as given ... is treated as so given ... at the time of the notification"

§§ `Section 387A(4) and (5): what the notification must say, and a notice accessible for only part of the period`

-- src:27145 | (4) A notice of a meeting given for the purposes of subsection (2)(d)
-- src:27146 | must specify such matters or information as may be required for a
-- src:27147 | notice of that type under any other provision of this Act or the
-- src:27148 | constitution of that company.
@ref s 387A(4) (src:27145-27148)
GIVEN `the notice is given for the purposes of subsection (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the matters or information required for a notice of that type under any other provision of this Act or the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387A(4) the notice specifies the matters or information that the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the notice is given for the purposes of subsection (2)(d)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice of a meeting given for the purposes of subsection (2)(d)"
    ELSE (IF `the notice specifies the matters or information required for a notice of that type under any other provision of this Act or the constitution of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify such matters or information as may be required for a notice of that type" (a duty: the provision's own question)

-- src:27152 | (5) Nothing in subsection (2) invalidates the proceedings of a
-- src:27153 | meeting where —
-- src:27155 | (a) any notice of a meeting that is required to be published and
-- src:27156 | remain accessible as mentioned in paragraph (e) of that
-- src:27157 | subsection is published and remains accessible for a part,
-- src:27158 | but not all, of the period mentioned in that paragraph; and
-- src:27160 | (b) the failure to publish and make accessible that notice
-- src:27161 | throughout that period is wholly attributable to
-- src:27162 | circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have
-- src:27163 | expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 387A(5) (src:27152-27163)
GIVEN `the notice of a meeting that is required to be published and remain accessible as mentioned in subsection (2)(e) is published and remains accessible for a part, but not all, of the period mentioned in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to publish and make accessible that notice throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387A(5) subsection (2) does not invalidate the proceedings of the meeting` MEANS
    IF    `the notice of a meeting that is required to be published and remain accessible as mentioned in subsection (2)(e) is published and remains accessible for a part, but not all, of the period mentioned in that paragraph`
       AND `the failure to publish and make accessible that notice throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (2) invalidates the proceedings of a meeting where (a) ...; and (b) ..."; the subsection does not say that the proceedings are invalidated where it does not apply (fork F-387A-5)

§§ `Section 387A(6) and (7): taking advantage despite the constitution; the current address`

-- src:27165 | (6) A company may, despite any provision to the contrary in its
-- src:27166 | constitution, take advantage of subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5).
@ref s 387A(6) (src:27165-27166)
GIVEN `the subsection the company wishes to take advantage of is subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5) of section 387A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company contains a provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387A(6) the company may take advantage of the subsection despite its constitution` MEANS
    IF `the subsection the company wishes to take advantage of is subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5) of section 387A`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the answer is the same whether or not `the constitution of the company contains a provision to the contrary`: "despite any provision to the contrary in its constitution"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, despite any provision to the contrary in its constitution, take advantage of subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)"

-- "the current address of a person of a company ... is a number or address used for electronic communication which (a) ...; and (b) ...":
-- read as a definition that says "is" (closed: fork F-387A-7).
-- src:27170 | (7) For the purposes of this section and section 387B, the current
-- src:27171 | address of a person of a company, in relation to any notice or
-- src:27172 | document, is a number or address used for electronic communication
-- src:27173 | which —
-- src:27175 | (a) has been notified by the person in writing to the company
-- src:27176 | as one at which that notice or document may be sent to the
-- src:27177 | person; and
-- src:27182 | (b) the company has no reason to believe that that notice or
-- src:27183 | document sent to the person at that address will not reach
-- src:27184 | the person.
@ref s 387A(7) (src:27170-27184)
GIVEN `the question arises for the purposes of section 387A or section 387B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number or address used for electronic communication has been notified by the person in writing to the company as one at which that notice or document may be sent to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no reason to believe that that notice or document sent to the person at that address will not reach the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387A(7) the number or address is the current address of the person of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the question arises for the purposes of section 387A or section 387B`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this section and section 387B"
    ELSE (IF    `the number or address used for electronic communication has been notified by the person in writing to the company as one at which that notice or document may be sent to the person`
             AND `the company has no reason to believe that that notice or document sent to the person at that address will not reach the person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the current address of a person of a company ... is a number or address used for electronic communication which (a) has been notified ...; and (b) the company has no reason to believe ..." (a definition that says "is")

§ `Section 387B: electronic transmission of documents`

§§ `Section 387B(1) and (2): sending the document, or publishing it on a website`

-- src:27188 | 387B.—(1) Where any accounts, balance sheet, financial
-- src:27189 | statements, report or other document is required or permitted to be
-- src:27190 | sent under this Act or under the constitution of a company by the
-- src:27191 | company or the directors of the company to —
-- src:27193 | (a) a member of the company; or
-- src:27195 | (b) an officer or auditor of the company,
-- src:27197 | that document may be sent using electronic communications to the
-- src:27198 | current address of that person.
@ref s 387B(1) (src:27188-27198)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 387B(6)(a) kind of thing sent`
      `the document is required or permitted to be sent under this Act or under the constitution of the company by the company or the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is sent using electronic communications to the current address of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(1) the document may be sent using electronic communications to the current address of the person` MEANS
    IF `s 387B(6)(a) the thing is within the word document` kind EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 387B(6)(a) "a reference to a document does not include any of the following"
    ELSE (IF NOT (   `the document is required or permitted to be sent under this Act or under the constitution of the company by the company or the directors of the company`
                  AND (`the person is a member of the company` OR `the person is an officer or auditor of the company`))
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "Where" gate of the subsection (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-387B-1
          ELSE (IF `the document is sent using electronic communications to the current address of the person`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that document may be sent using electronic communications to the current address of that person"

-- src:27204 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a document is also treated as
-- src:27205 | sent to a person where —
-- src:27207 | (a) the company and that person have agreed in writing to the
-- src:27208 | person having access to documents on a website (instead of
-- src:27209 | their being sent to the person);
-- src:27211 | (b) the document is a document to which that agreement
-- src:27212 | applies;
-- src:27214 | (c) the document is published on the website such that it is or
-- src:27215 | can be made legible; and
-- src:27217 | (d) that person is notified, in a manner for the time being
-- src:27218 | agreed for that purpose between the person and the
-- src:27219 | company, of —
-- src:27221 | (i) the publication of the document on that website;
-- src:27223 | (ii) the address of that website; and
-- src:27225 | (iii) the place on that website where the document may be
-- src:27226 | accessed, and how it may be accessed.
@ref s 387B(2) (src:27204-27226)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 387B(6)(a) kind of thing sent`
      `the company and the person have agreed in writing to the person having access to documents on a website (instead of their being sent to the person)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a document to which that agreement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is published on the website such that it is or can be made legible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed for that purpose between the person and the company, of the publication of the document on that website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed for that purpose between the person and the company, of the address of that website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed for that purpose between the person and the company, of the place on that website where the document may be accessed, and how it may be accessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(2) the document is treated as sent to the person by publication on a website` MEANS
    IF `s 387B(6)(a) the thing is within the word document` kind EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 387B(6)(a) "a reference to a document does not include any of the following"
    ELSE (IF    `the company and the person have agreed in writing to the person having access to documents on a website (instead of their being sent to the person)`
             AND `the document is a document to which that agreement applies`
             AND `the document is published on the website such that it is or can be made legible`
             AND `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed for that purpose between the person and the company, of the publication of the document on that website`
             AND `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed for that purpose between the person and the company, of the address of that website`
             AND `the person is notified, in a manner for the time being agreed for that purpose between the person and the company, of the place on that website where the document may be accessed, and how it may be accessed`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a document is also treated as sent to a person where (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); the function is named for this route

§§ `Section 387B(3) and (4): documents that must be sent a number of days before a meeting`

-- "that document, if treated in accordance with subsection (2) as sent to any person, is treated as sent to the person not less than the
-- specified number of days before the date of a meeting if, and only if (a) ... beginning before the specified number of days before the date
-- of the meeting and ending with the conclusion of the meeting; and (b) the notification ... is given not less than the specified number of days before".
-- Fork F-387B-3: limb (a) is read literally, the period beginning strictly before the latest day (meeting date minus N days, sg-periods P5);
-- limb (b) is "not less than N days before", on or before that latest day.
-- src:27230 | (3) Where any provision of this Act or of the constitution of the
-- src:27231 | company requires any document to be sent to a person not less than a
-- src:27236 | specified number of days before a meeting, that document, if treated
-- src:27237 | in accordance with subsection (2) as sent to any person, is treated as
-- src:27238 | sent to the person not less than the specified number of days before
-- src:27239 | the date of a meeting if, and only if —
-- src:27241 | (a) the document is published on and remains accessible to
-- src:27242 | that person from the website throughout a period beginning
-- src:27243 | before the specified number of days before the date of the
-- src:27244 | meeting and ending with the conclusion of the meeting;
-- src:27245 | and
-- src:27247 | (b) the notification given for the purposes of subsection (2)(d)
-- src:27248 | is given not less than the specified number of days before
-- src:27249 | the date of the meeting.
@ref s 387B(3) (src:27230-27249)
GIVEN `the document is treated in accordance with subsection (2) as sent to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified number of days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period for which the document is published on and remains accessible to the person from the website` IS A DATE
      `the document remains accessible to the person from the website until the conclusion of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notification mentioned in subsection (2)(d) is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(3) the document is treated as sent to the person not less than the specified number of days before the date of the meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is treated in accordance with subsection (2) as sent to the person`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that document, if treated in accordance with subsection (2) as sent to any person"
    ELSE (IF    (`the first day of the period for which the document is published on and remains accessible to the person from the website` LESS THAN `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date of the meeting` `the specified number of days` Days)
             AND `the document remains accessible to the person from the website until the conclusion of the meeting`
             AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the notification mentioned in subsection (2)(d) is given` `the date of the meeting` `the specified number of days` Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if" (a) and (b)

-- src:27255 | (4) Nothing in subsection (3) invalidates the proceedings of a
-- src:27256 | meeting where —
-- src:27258 | (a) any document that is required to be published and remain
-- src:27259 | accessible as mentioned in paragraph (a) of that subsection
-- src:27260 | is published and remains accessible for a part, but not all,
-- src:27261 | of the period mentioned in that paragraph; and
-- src:27263 | (b) the failure to publish and make accessible that document
-- src:27264 | throughout that period is wholly attributable to
-- src:27265 | circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have
-- src:27266 | expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 387B(4) (src:27255-27266)
GIVEN `the document that is required to be published and remain accessible as mentioned in subsection (3)(a) is published and remains accessible for a part, but not all, of the period mentioned in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to publish and make accessible that document throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(4) subsection (3) does not invalidate the proceedings of the meeting` MEANS
    IF    `the document that is required to be published and remain accessible as mentioned in subsection (3)(a) is published and remains accessible for a part, but not all, of the period mentioned in that paragraph`
       AND `the failure to publish and make accessible that document throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances which it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (3) invalidates the proceedings of a meeting where (a) ...; and (b) ..." (fork F-387A-5, the same reading as s 387A(5))

-- src:27268 | (5) A company may, despite any provision to the contrary in its
-- src:27269 | constitution, take advantage of subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4).
@ref s 387B(5) (src:27268-27269)
GIVEN `the subsection the company wishes to take advantage of is subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4) of section 387B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company contains a provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(5) the company may take advantage of the subsection despite its constitution` MEANS
    IF `the subsection the company wishes to take advantage of is subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4) of section 387B`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the answer is the same whether or not `the constitution of the company contains a provision to the contrary`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, despite any provision to the contrary in its constitution, take advantage of subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4)"

§§ `Section 387B(6): what "document" and "sending" mean in ss 387B, 387C and 387D`

-- src:27271 | (6) For the purposes of this section and sections 387C and 387D —
-- src:27273 | (a) a reference to a document does not include any of the
-- src:27274 | following:
-- src:27276 | (i) a share certificate;
-- src:27278 | (ii) a debenture;
-- src:27280 | (iii) a certificate of any other interest in a company;
-- src:27285 | (iv) an instrument of transfer of any share, debenture or
-- src:27286 | other interest in a company; and
@ref s 387B(6) (src:27271-27286)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 387B(6)(a) kind of thing sent`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(6)(a) the thing is within the word document` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 387B(6)(a)(i) a share certificate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to a document does not include ... (i) a share certificate"
    WHEN `s 387B(6)(a)(ii) a debenture` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) a debenture"
    WHEN `s 387B(6)(a)(iii) a certificate of any other interest in a company` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iii) a certificate of any other interest in a company"
    WHEN `s 387B(6)(a)(iv) an instrument of transfer of any share, debenture or other interest in a company` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iv) an instrument of transfer of any share, debenture or other interest in a company"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the paragraph says what the word does not include and does not say what it does

-- src:27271 | (6) For the purposes of this section and sections 387C and 387D —
-- src:27288 | (b) a reference to the sending of a document includes the
-- src:27289 | circulation, delivery, despatching, depositing, forwarding,
-- src:27290 | furnishing, giving, issuing, serving, submission,
-- src:27291 | transmitting or supply of that document.
@ref s 387B(6) (src:27271-27291)
GIVEN `the act is a circulation, delivery, despatching, depositing, forwarding, furnishing, giving, issuing, serving, submission, transmitting or supply of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387B(6)(b) the act is within the word sending` MEANS
    IF `the act is a circulation, delivery, despatching, depositing, forwarding, furnishing, giving, issuing, serving, submission, transmitting or supply of the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to the sending of a document includes the circulation, delivery, ..."

§ `Section 387C: electronic transmission in accordance with the constitution`

§§ `Section 387C(2) and (3): implied consent and deemed consent`

-- src:27312 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a member has given implied
-- src:27313 | consent if the constitution of the company —
-- src:27315 | (a) provides for the use of electronic communications;
-- src:27317 | (b) specifies the manner in which electronic communications
-- src:27318 | is to be used; and
-- src:27320 | (c) provides that the member agrees to receive such notice or
-- src:27321 | document by way of such electronic communications and
-- src:27322 | does not have a right to elect to receive a physical copy of
-- src:27323 | such notice or document.
@ref s 387C(2) (src:27312-27323)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company provides for the use of electronic communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company specifies the manner in which electronic communications is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company provides that the member agrees to receive such notice or document by way of such electronic communications and does not have a right to elect to receive a physical copy of such notice or document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387C(2) the member has given implied consent` MEANS
    IF    `the constitution of the company provides for the use of electronic communications`
       AND `the constitution of the company specifies the manner in which electronic communications is to be used`
       AND `the constitution of the company provides that the member agrees to receive such notice or document by way of such electronic communications and does not have a right to elect to receive a physical copy of such notice or document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member has given implied consent if the constitution of the company (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (a condition the text introduces with "if"; marginal reading (a))

-- src:27327 | (3) For the purposes of this section, but subject to regulations
-- src:27328 | mentioned in subsection (4), a member is deemed to have consented
-- src:27329 | if —
-- src:27331 | (a) the member was by written notice given an opportunity to
-- src:27332 | elect, within such period of time specified in the notice,
-- src:27337 | whether to receive the notice or document by way of
-- src:27338 | electronic communications or as a physical copy; and
-- src:27340 | (b) the member failed to make an election within the time so
-- src:27341 | specified.
@ref s 387C(3) (src:27327-27341)
GIVEN `the member was by written notice given an opportunity to elect, within such period of time specified in the notice, whether to receive the notice or document by way of electronic communications or as a physical copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member failed to make an election within the time so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations made under section 411 provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387C(3) the member is deemed to have consented` MEANS
    IF `regulations made under section 411 provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "but subject to regulations mentioned in subsection (4)"; the regulations are not among the sources
    ELSE (IF    `the member was by written notice given an opportunity to elect, within such period of time specified in the notice, whether to receive the notice or document by way of electronic communications or as a physical copy`
             AND `the member failed to make an election within the time so specified`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member is deemed to have consented if (a) ...; and (b) ..." (a condition the text introduces with "if"; marginal reading (a))

§§ `Section 387C(1): sending with the member's consent`

-- Calls (2) and (3) with their facts, so the person need not know the legal test for implied or deemed consent.
-- src:27299 | 387C.—(1) Despite sections 387A and 387B, where a notice of
-- src:27300 | meeting or any accounts, balance sheet, financial statements, report
-- src:27301 | or other document is required or permitted to be sent under this Act or
-- src:27302 | under the constitution of a company by the company or the directors
-- src:27303 | of the company to a member of the company, that notice or document
-- src:27304 | may be sent using electronic communications with the express,
-- src:27305 | implied or deemed consent of the member in accordance with the
-- src:27306 | constitution of the company.
@ref s 387C(1) (src:27299-27306)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 387B(6)(a) kind of thing sent`
      `the notice of a meeting or the document is required or permitted to be sent under this Act or under the constitution of the company by the company or the directors of the company to a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has given express consent to receive the notice or document by electronic communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company provides for the use of electronic communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company specifies the manner in which electronic communications is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company provides that the member agrees to receive such notice or document by way of such electronic communications and does not have a right to elect to receive a physical copy of such notice or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member was by written notice given an opportunity to elect, within such period of time specified in the notice, whether to receive the notice or document by way of electronic communications or as a physical copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member failed to make an election within the time so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is in accordance with the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations made under section 411 exclude the notice or document from the application of section 387C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387C(1) the notice or document may be sent to the member using electronic communications with the member's consent` MEANS
    IF `s 387B(6)(a) the thing is within the word document` kind EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 387B(6)(a) "a reference to a document does not include any of the following" applies to s 387C
    ELSE (IF NOT `the notice of a meeting or the document is required or permitted to be sent under this Act or under the constitution of the company by the company or the directors of the company to a member of the company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "where" gate of the subsection (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-387C-1
          ELSE (IF `regulations made under section 411 exclude the notice or document from the application of section 387C`
                THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (4)(a) lets the Minister exclude a notice or document from the section; the regulations are not among the sources
                ELSE (IF `the consent is in accordance with the constitution of the company` AND (`the member has given express consent to receive the notice or document by electronic communications` OR implied OR deemed)
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent using electronic communications with the express, implied or deemed consent of the member in accordance with the constitution"
    WHERE
        implied MEANS `s 387C(2) the member has given implied consent` `the constitution of the company provides for the use of electronic communications` `the constitution of the company specifies the manner in which electronic communications is to be used` `the constitution of the company provides that the member agrees to receive such notice or document by way of such electronic communications and does not have a right to elect to receive a physical copy of such notice or document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        deemed MEANS `s 387C(3) the member is deemed to have consented` `the member was by written notice given an opportunity to elect, within such period of time specified in the notice, whether to receive the notice or document by way of electronic communications or as a physical copy` `the member failed to make an election within the time so specified` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Section 387D: documents sent to the company or a director by a member, officer or auditor`

-- src:27365 | 387D. Where any document is required or permitted to be sent
-- src:27366 | under this Act by a member, officer or auditor of the company to the
-- src:27367 | company or a director of the company, that document may be sent
-- src:27368 | using electronic communications to the company or the director if the
-- src:27369 | member, officer or auditor (as the case may be) and the company or
-- src:27370 | director (as the case may be) have agreed, generally or specifically,
-- src:27371 | that the document may be sent in that manner, and that agreement has
-- src:27372 | not been revoked.
@ref s 387D (src:27365-27372)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 387B(6)(a) kind of thing sent`
      `the document is required or permitted under this Act to be sent by a member, officer or auditor of the company to the company or a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender and the company or director have agreed, generally or specifically, that the document may be sent in that manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that agreement has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 387D the document may be sent using electronic communications to the company or the director` MEANS
    IF `s 387B(6)(a) the thing is within the word document` kind EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 387B(6)(a) "a reference to a document does not include any of the following" applies to s 387D
    ELSE (IF NOT `the document is required or permitted under this Act to be sent by a member, officer or auditor of the company to the company or a director of the company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "Where" gate of the section (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-387D-1
          ELSE (IF `the sender and the company or director have agreed, generally or specifically, that the document may be sent in that manner` AND (NOT `that agreement has been revoked`)
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent using electronic communications ... if the member, officer or auditor ... have agreed ..., and that agreement has not been revoked" is an "if" gate on a grant, not "only if" (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)
